('34c4bd',3.5,'Number Theory',['Integer bounds','Products'],'If every absolute value is at least two and n≥3, dividing the sum by the product gives 1≤n/2^(n−1)<1; a factor ±1 therefore makes the requested product zero. The two-variable case gives (2,2).'),
