statements={
'f2af41':r'In triangle $ABC$, $\angle B=2\angle C$. Let $X,Y$ be the midpoints of the arcs $AB,BC$ not containing the remaining vertex. The internal bisector from $B$ meets $AC$ at $L$. If $XL\perp YL$, determine the triangle’s angles.',
'16c55b':r'Three circles $\Gamma_1,\Gamma_2,\Gamma_3$ are pairwise externally tangent. Write $P_2=\Gamma_1\cap\Gamma_3$ and $P_1=\Gamma_2\cap\Gamma_3$. Choose a diameter $AB$ of $\Gamma_3$ such that $ABP_1P_2$ is convex. Let $X\ne P_2$ lie on $AP_2\cap\Gamma_1$, let $Y\ne P_1$ lie on $BP_1\cap\Gamma_2$, and put $Z=AP_1\cap BP_2$. Prove that $X,Y,Z$ are collinear.',
'f5511d':r'Let $AB=AC$ and $\angle BAC>90^\circ$. On the circle centred at $A$ through $B,C$, let $D$ be the second intersection with $BM$, where $M$ is the midpoint of $AC$. Let $E\ne B$ be the circle point for which $BE\perp AC$, and set $N=DE\cap AC$. Prove $AN=2AB$.',
'67c069':r'For real numbers $x_1,\ldots,x_n$, put $d=\max_{i,j}|x_i-x_j|$ and $S=\sum_{i<j}|x_i-x_j|$. Prove $$(n-1)d\le S\le\frac{n^2d}{4},$$ and determine equality in each bound.',
'0f17c9':r'Let $k,n$ be positive integers and let $A$ contain $2n$ distinct integers. For each $a\in A$, let $p_a$ count the $b\in A$ for which $b-a\equiv k\pmod {2k}$. Find the greatest possible value of $\sum_{a\in A}p_a^2$.',
'c765b1':r'Fix $n\ge3$. For an unknown multiset of $n$ positive integers, list its $2^n-1$ nonempty indexed subset sums in increasing order, with repetitions retained. Prove that one can choose $2^{n-2}+1$ positions, depending only on $n$, whose values always determine the original multiset.',
'c63ac9':r'Each edge of a complete graph on $n\ge3$ vertices is assigned a positive integer. In every triangle, one label equals the sum of the other two. What is the minimum possible number of distinct labels?',
'a41d6d':r'For which integers $n\ge2$ can an $n\times n$ array be formed from rows that are permutations of $1,\ldots,n$, so that the numbers of occurrences of $i$ in column $i$, for $i=1,\ldots,n$, are themselves a permutation of $1,\ldots,n$?',
'db5165':r'Positive real numbers $x_1,\ldots,x_n$ sum to one, where $n\ge2$. Put $r_k=x_k/(1+x_1+\cdots+x_k)$. Determine the largest possible value of $\min_k r_k$ and the smallest possible value of $\max_k r_k$.',
'462ae5':r'Determine all nonnegative integers $n$ for which $2^n-n^2+1$ is a square of an integer.',
'7c9b7e':r'Find all positive integer triples $(a,b,c)$ such that each of $ab+c$, $bc+a$, and $ca+b$ is a power of two.',
'abf430':r'Ten points in the plane have no three collinear. Colour every segment joining two points so that any two segments of the same colour intersect, possibly at an endpoint. What is the least number of colours attainable over all such point configurations and colourings?',
'90f8ad':r'Let $\mathcal F$ contain at most $n$ distinct subsets of $\{1,\ldots,n\}$, where $n\ge3$. Assume there is a simple undirected graph on these labels such that, for distinct $i,j$, the edge $ij$ exists exactly when $i$ belongs to $j$ members of $\mathcal F$. Maximize $\sum_{F\in\mathcal F}|F|$.',
'510aa3':r'In a convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, the circles with diameters $AB$ and $CD$ touch externally at $M$, which is not the intersection of the diagonals. Let $K\ne M$ be the intersection of $(AMC)$ with the line joining $M$ to the midpoint of $AB$. Define $L\ne M$ analogously using $(BMD)$ and the midpoint of $CD$. Prove $|MK-ML|=|AB-CD|$.',
'3a568a':r'Let $ABC$ be acute with $AB<AC$, circumcenter $O$, and orthocenter $H$. Reflect $A$ in $BC$ to obtain $A^{*}$. The parallel to $BC$ through $O$ meets $AC$ at $F$. The tangent at $F$ to $(BFC)$ meets the parallel to $BC$ through $A^{*}$ at $M$. On ray $AB$, choose $K$ with $AK=4AB$. Prove that $H$ lies on the circle with diameter $KM$.',
'23dcce':r'Some cells of an $n\times n$ board contain monsters. A path from the bottom-left cell to the top-right cell uses only upward and rightward moves between cells and must avoid monsters. Find the fewest monsters for which exactly one such path exists.',
'7a9f2d':r'A sequence of positive rational numbers satisfies $$a_{k+1}=\frac{a_k^2+a_{k+2}^2}{a_k+a_{k+2}}\qquad(k\ge1).$$ Prove that the sequence is constant.',
'51a69a':r'In a scalene acute triangle $ABC$, let $I,O$ be the incenter and circumcenter. Let $X$ be the midpoint of arc $AC$ containing $B$, and $Y$ the midpoint of arc $AB$ containing $C$. Put $D=AI\cap BC$, $E=DX\cap CI$, and $F=DY\cap BI$. Prove that $FX,EY,IO$ concur at a point on the external bisector of $\angle BAC$.',
'34b81d':r'Initially $n\ge2$ distinct real numbers $c_1,\ldots,c_n$ are on a board. If their current sum is $s$, one may replace two entries $a,b$ with $$\frac{(a+b)(s+1)-a^2-ab-b^2}{s-a-b+1}$$ whenever the denominator is nonzero. Prove that some sequence of $n-1$ legal moves leaves one number, and express that number in terms of the original entries.',
'10bf37':r'Classify the polynomials $P$ with integer coefficients such that $0\le P(n)\le n!$ for every integer $n\ge0$.',
'd02b1f':r'A nonempty set $S$ of positive integers has this property: for all positive integers $a,b,c$, whenever $ab+bc+ca\in S$, both $a+b+c$ and $abc$ belong to $S$. Suppose $S$ contains an integer $N\ge160$ with $N\not\equiv2\pmod4$. Prove that $S$ contains all positive integers.'}
